- [builder:claude-b] Goal seek and What matters most (was Sensitivity) stop treating a higher return as a fix: the return the plan would need is one short grey line set against forecasts for the plan's own mix, with no button, its detail one tap away, and no figure when growth does not matter; the saving card names a 401(k) with nothing going in and gives the amount that works typed there (up to the yearly limit, the rest into other savings); the Social Security card on a short plan says whether that age alone gets there or when the money would then run out; the retirement card is never "room to spare" while the money runs short; What matters most says "We don't know yet" with no savings on file, shows the five numbers that matter most first with the rest and each row's detail one tap away, shows how much you save in dollars when nothing goes in, and its headline says what to do; Legacy goals no longer lists the return.
